<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Blutritt</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Blood Ride of Weingarten</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Blutritt, or Blood Ride, is a mounted procession held each year on the Friday after Ascension Day at Weingarten in upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swabia">Swabia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. Thousands of riders accompany a relic of the Holy Blood, believed to contain the blood of Christ, which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judith-of-flanders">Judith of Flanders</a> gave to Weingarten Abbey in 1094. It is one of the largest equestrian processions in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/blutritt.jpg" alt="Blutritt" width="320" height="219" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joseph Bayer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Weingarten_Blutritt_Beyer.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
